    "verdict": "No standard abelian T^6 orbifold in the Reffert/LRSS table has |chi|/2 = 3 (the smallest value in the table is 24).  The C4-compatible Z4, Z8, Z12 and Z2xZ4, Z4xZ4 entries all give 24, 60 or 90, not 3.  Direct DHVW sums give chi=72 for T^6/Z3 (36 generations) and chi=96 for T^6/(Z2xZ2) (48 generations).  The Tian\u2013Yau manifold does have three generations, but it is a different construction (a free Z3 quotient) and is not forced by the conoid or its C4.  A magnetized T^2\u00d7T^2\u00d7T^2 index equals 3 only if one flux is already 3."
  },
