    "verdict": "The flux derivative of the spectral action (truncated or finite-part) vanishes only at M=0, for any positive area, as long as the Yang-Mills coefficient is not tuned to zero.  There is no interior extremum that selects M=3.  At fixed M\u22600 a stationary area can exist, but it is proportional to |M| and depends on the underived Wilson coefficients and on \u039b; it is not a unique geometric output.  At M=0 the action is linear in A, so A is either driven to a boundary or is a flat direction if the linear coefficient is tuned to zero.  \u03c4 does not enter.  The tip contributes a boundary term proportional to 8\u2113_0 A, which shifts the linear coefficient in A but does not create a preferred integer flux.  The four nodes are not assigned an invented Seeley contribution."
  },
